r\\\" shown). Set Cards view sort to Task Name (ascending, alphabetical order). Switched back to Table view: it still showed \\\"Sorted by Priority (descending)\\\" with the same descending order, confirming table and card sort selections are stored independently.\"}, {\"item_id\": \"FT-6\", \"verdict\": \"FAIL\", \"issue\": \"No filter feature is exposed in the UI\", \"actual\": \"Searched the entire toolbar and table/card views for any filter control (button text, aria-label, icon, class name, or on-hover affordance containing \\\"filter\\\"). Only Fields, Sort, Table/Cards view toggle, Add Entry, and a free-text Search box exist. No UI element lets a user define field-specific filter criteria (e.g., \\\"Priority > 2\\\" or \\\"Completed = Yes\\\"). The feature described by FT-6 could not be located or exercised.\", \"evidence\": \"DOM query for buttons/elements with \\\"filter\\\" in text, aria-label, id, or class returned zero matches; body innerText contains no occurrence of the word \\\"filter\\\".\"}, {\"item_id\": \"FT-7\", \"verdict\": \"PASS\", \"issue\": null, \"actual\": null, \"evidence\": \"With no sort active, used the keyboard-accessible drag handle (Space to pick up, Arrow keys to move, Space to drop) to move \\\"Design new landing page\\\" from position 1 to position 2 in Table view (order became Review, Design, Update, Prepare, Team sync, Test Entry Alpha). Switched to Cards view: order was still the original insertion order (unaffected by table reorder), confirming independent state. Reordered Cards view (moved Design new landing page to position 5). Switched back to Table view: table still showed its own earlier reorder (Review, Design, Update, Prepare, Team sync, Test Entry Alpha) unaffected by the card reorder, confirming each view keeps its own manual order.\"}, {\"item_id\": \"FT-19\", \"verdict\": \"FAIL\", \"issue\": \"No import feature is exposed in the UI\", \"actual\": \"Searched the whole app (toolbar, Configure Fields dialog, table/card views) for an import control. The Configure Fields dialog only shows a note stating \\\"Configure fields before importing data\\\" but provides no actual Import button, file picker, or paste-data control anywhere in the app. A DOM-wide text search for \\\"import\\\" (case-insensitive) found no matches besides that static note. The import capability described by FT-19 could not be located or exercised.\", \"evidence\": \"document.body.innerText search for /import/i matched nothing outside the static help text; no Import button found among toolbar or dialog buttons.\"}, {\"item_id\": \"CS-8\", \"verdict\": \"PASS\", \"issue\": null, \"actual\": null, \"evidence\": \"Priority field in Add Entry form is rendered as a native input[type=number] spinbutton. Attempting to type a non-numeric string (\\\"abc\\\") into it was rejected by the control itself (Playwright reported \\\"Cannot type text into input[type=number]\\\"), so no non-numeric value can ever be entered/saved for that field.\"}, {\"item_id\": \"CS-9\", \"verdict\": \"PASS\", \"issue\": null, \"actual\": null, \"evidence\": \"Due Date field in Add Entry form is a native input[type=date]. Attempting to fill an invalid calendar date (\\\"2026-13-45\\\", month 13 / day 45) was rejected by the control itself (\\\"Malformed value\\\" error), preventing an invalid date from ever being entered/saved.\"}, {\"item_id\": \"CS-11\", \"verdict\": \"PASS\", \"issue\": null, \"actual\": null, \"evidence\": \"Before and after sorting by Priority (ascending then descending), entry count remained 6 and each entry's Task Name/Priority/Due Date/Completed/Notes values were unchanged, only row order changed.\"}, {\"item_id\": \"CS-12\", \"verdict\": \"FAIL\", \"issue\": \"No filter feature is exposed in the UI\", \"actual\": \"Since no filter control exists anywhere in the app (see FT-6 finding), it is impossible to define active filter criteria, so the requirement that filtering include exactly the matching entries and clearing