ign new landing page\\\": \\\"Jan 15, 2026\\\") returned 0 results (\\\"0 entries matching \\\\\\\"Jan 15\\\\\\\"\\\"). Searching \\\"Yes\\\" (the exact Completed text shown for several entries) also returned 0 results. Search appears to only match the Task Name/Notes text fields and internal raw values, not the human-readable formatted date or checkbox labels users see in the views.\", \"evidence\": \"Footer showed \\\"0 entries matching \\\\\\\"Jan 15\\\\\\\"\\\" and \\\"0 entries matching \\\\\\\"Yes\\\\\\\"\\\" despite those exact strings being visibly rendered in the table for multiple entries.\"}, {\"item_id\": \"IX-17\", \"verdict\": \"PASS\", \"issue\": null, \"actual\": null, \"evidence\": \"Typed lowercase \\\"design\\\" into the search box; result narrowed to the single entry \\\"Design new landing page\\\" (case-insensitive substring match) and the footer count updated to '1 entry matching \\\"design\\\"'. Clicking the clear (x) button in the search box restored all 6 entries.\"}, {\"item_id\": \"IX-18\", \"verdict\": \"PASS\", \"issue\": null, \"actual\": null, \"evidence\": \"Clicking \\\"Priority\\\" in the Sort menu immediately reordered the table rows ascending (1,1,2,2,3,42) and displayed \\\"Sorted by Priority (ascending)\\\" with the Sort button relabeled \\\"Priority\\\" (active). Clicking the Priority column header toggled to descending (42,3,2,2,1,1) and footer updated to \\\"Sorted by Priority (descending)\\\". App remained fully interactive afterward (menus, add entry, view toggle all functioned).\"}]}"
